                "xpath": "/html[1]/body[1]/div[4]/div[2]/div[1]/div[13]/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[3]/div[1]",
                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Hebrew lesson 11: Dagesh and Kaf Sofit](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110529-2762-0139-0000-3a0eb0c9944e:8)\nKaf sofit (ך) is the special final form of the Hebrew letter [Kaf](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Kaf/kaf.html) , used only at the end of a word.[[1]](https://akhlah.com/hebrew/aleph-bet/kaf-haf-kaf-sofit/)[[2]](https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbD7wFFtQ01/)\n\n### Key Facts About Kaf Sofit\n\n- **Letter Shape** : It looks like the regular letter Kaf, but it has a long tail that drops below the baseline.[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Kaf/kaf.html)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=45Qq97MSvB8&t=4)\n- **Pronunciation** : It makes a \"ch\" sound like the \"ch\" in the Scottish word *loch* or German *bach* . It never uses a hard \"k\" sound.[[1]](https://www.hebrewpod101.com/lesson/hebrew-alphabet-made-easy-7-kaf)[[2]](https://www.etz-hayim.com/hebrew/letters_and_vowels/kaf.php)\n- **Gematria (Number value)** : In standard counting, Kaf is 20, but the final form (Kaf sofit) represents **500** in extended numerical values.[[1]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaph)[[2]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Kaf/kaf.html)\n- **Rule of Sofit** : Hebrew has five letters that change shape at the end of a word. Kaf sofit is one of these final letters.[[1]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cKMCHUKnjoo)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/amHRs1oAtCo)[[3]](https://akhlah.com/hebrew/aleph-bet/kaf-haf-kaf-sofit/)\n\nIf you want, I can show you:\n\n- **The other four final (sofit) letters** in Hebrew\n- **Examples of words** that end with a kaf sofit\n\nLet me know how you'd like to continue!",
